<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#AdaptationFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Measure to decrease the negative consequences of an impact by addressing one or more vulnerabilities or impacting mechanisms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#HazardFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "https://www.preventionweb.net/understanding-disaster-risk/component-risk/hazard. Extensive classification: UNDRR 2021 (https://www.undrr.org/publication/hazard-definition-and-classification-review-technical-report);  Climate related hazard indices for Europe (https://www.eea.europa.eu/publications/europes-changing-climate-hazards-1/what-will-the-future-bring/projected-changes-in-climate-related/view - Crespi et al., 2020)"@en .
_:n2a5f57d8c3ed4ae6977efd3687c41543b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:n2a5f57d8c3ed4ae6977efd3687c41543b6 .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ich#HazardFactor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Climatic influence, climatic or non-climatic event or trend that may constitute a hazard to the exposed assets and systems and result in an impact and possibly a risk (with damage or loss)."@en .
